## 🎯 Overview

Azure Portal lets you **export existing resources** as ARM templates. But ARM JSON is verbose and hard to read. **Bicep** is a cleaner, modern alternative. This guide shows you how to:

1. Export any Azure resource as an ARM template
2. Convert (decompile) it into Bicep
3. Review and customize the Bicep file before deployment

---

## 📥 Step 1: Export the ARM Template from Azure

### 1.1 Log in to Azure Portal

Go to [https://portal.azure.com](https://portal.azure.com) and sign in.

### 1.2 Select the Resource

Navigate to the resource you want to convert — for example, an **Azure Storage Account**.

### 1.3 Go to Export Template

In the **left-hand menu**, scroll down to the **Automation** section and click **Export template**.

### 1.4 Download the Template

Click the **Download** button. This saves a `.zip` file containing:

- `template.json` — The ARM template
- `parameters.json` — The parameters file

### 1.5 Extract the Archive

Extract the downloaded `.zip` file to a local folder on your computer.

**Folder structure after extraction:**

```
exported-template/
├── template.json
└── parameters.json
```

---

## 🔄 Step 2: Decompile to Bicep

You can decompile using **either** of the two methods below.

---

### Method A: Using VS Code (GUI)

#### A.1 Install the Bicep Extension

1. Open **Visual Studio Code**
2. Press **`Ctrl + Shift + X`** to open the Extensions panel
3. Search for **`Bicep`**
4. Install the official **Bicep** extension by Microsoft

#### A.2 Open the ARM Template

Open the extracted `template.json` file in VS Code.

#### A.3 Decompile into Bicep

**Right-click** anywhere inside the file editor and choose:

```
Decompile into Bicep
```

#### A.4 Result

VS Code will automatically generate the corresponding **`template.bicep`** file in the same folder.

---

### Method B: Using Azure CLI / Command Prompt

#### B.1 Verify Azure CLI Installation

Open a terminal and run:

```bash
az --version
```

If Azure CLI is not installed, download it from:  
[https://learn.microsoft.com/cli/azure/install-azure-cli](https://learn.microsoft.com/cli/azure/install-azure-cli)

#### B.2 Install the Bicep CLI Component

```bash
az bicep install
```

Verify installation:

```bash
az bicep version
```

#### B.3 Navigate to the Extracted Folder

```bash
cd path/to/extracted-folder
```

#### B.4 Decompile the ARM Template

```bash
az bicep decompile --file template.json
```

#### B.5 Result

A new file named **`template.bicep`** will be generated in the same directory.

**Folder structure after decompile:**

```
exported-template/
├── template.json
├── parameters.json
└── template.bicep       ← Generated
```

